# Codex Task Execution

- The selected Task is the execution authority.
- Locked central documents referenced by the Task are business and product authority.
- Frontend Tasks live under `Docs/Tasks/Front/`; execute only the explicitly selected Task.
- Read only `Required Context` initially. Do not scan all `Docs/` or the repository.
- Implement only `Scope`; respect `Out of Scope`.
- Do not infer business behavior or perform unrelated refactoring, cleanup, or comments.
- Reuse existing components, patterns, design-system rules, and architecture; do not create a duplicate component when a suitable existing component exists.
- Make the minimum correct diff.
- Respect `Model Tier: DEFAULT | STRONG`; use `DEFAULT` unless Codex explicitly assigns `STRONG`.
- Apply only relevant production gates: TypeScript, build, lint, responsive/mobile behavior, accessibility, loading/error/empty states, performance, SEO/rendering, API contract, and design-system consistency.
- Run the Task `Verification` and do not claim completion when it fails.

Stop and report exactly one of:

`MISSING_DECISION` · `DOCUMENT_CONFLICT` · `IMPLEMENTATION_DRIFT`
